# E596 draft: legacy CBC archive omits plaintext length; round-trip mismatches on partial blocks.
id:                     E596
trigger_tool:           test|qemu-aarch64|conan
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        cmp: EOF on plain after byte [0-9]+|sectar AES CBC output differs from original C source
severity:               2
category:               portability, testing, data-corruption
match_keywords:         sectar, CBC, plaintext length, partial block, zero padding, round-trip, cmp EOF, decrypted tail, consumer source, block size
title:                  Legacy AES CBC file format loses original plaintext length on partial blocks
root_cause:             sectar 1.02 writes only the keyfile name and a fixed-width 32-bit block size followed by AES CBC ciphertext. For the final partial 256-bit block it encrypts a zero-filled input buffer but does not serialize the original byte count; decrypt always writes a whole block. A 33-byte plaintext therefore decrypts to 64 bytes and byte-for-byte comparisons fail despite successful AES operation.
affected_scope:         Legacy block encryption CLI or custom archive formats that write full final blocks without storing plaintext length or a removable padding length; observed in sectar 1.02 on OHOS aarch64 and reproducible on other platforms.
verification_cmd:       d=$(mktemp -d /root/tmp/sectar-kb-XXXXXX); cd "$d" && printf '%064d' 0 > key && printf 'sectar OHOS cross-platform test!!' > plain && qemu-aarch64 /root/tmp/sectar-ohos -k key -e -o enc.star plain && qemu-aarch64 /root/tmp/sectar-ohos -k key -d -o dec enc.star && ! cmp plain dec && printf 'sectar OHOS cross-platform test!' > plain && qemu-aarch64 /root/tmp/sectar-ohos -k key -e -o enc.star plain && qemu-aarch64 /root/tmp/sectar-ohos -k key -d -o dec enc.star && cmp plain dec
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           preserve-format-and-align-consumer-input
rec_description:        For compatibility tests of the original archive format use a full 32-byte multiple input, run installed CLI encrypt and decrypt, compare bytes and build and execute the decrypted consumer program. Record that arbitrary-length round-trip is not lossless; do not claim cryptographic integrity or pad removal.
rec_command:            python3 scripts/ohc-run.py conan-verify sectar 1.02
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               consumer-test
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      versioned-format-upgrade
fallback_description:   A future format revision can encode plaintext length or self-describing padding with an explicit format version; never silently alter the 1.02 wire format.
fallback_command:       true
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:           format-design
forbid_1_pattern:       cmp.*plain.*dec.*\|\|.*true
forbid_1_reason:        Discarding the comparison failure hides the actual non-lossless final-block behaviour.
forbid_1_consequence:   Non-aligned input may be reported as an exact round-trip although extra NUL bytes remain.
similar_to:             [E595]
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E596-draft-88CF.md
last_updated:           2026-09-26
source_event:           sectar 1.02 OHOS aarch64 qemu encrypt/decrypt test: 33-byte input cmp reports EOF on plain; 32-byte input cmp passes.
authors:                nyaco3 <aqjCItYW1QmEJQuF.gcw_XDpqZ8sO@noreply.gitcode.com>
source_pr:              pending
source_commit:          pending
draft:                  true
contributor_id:         88CF
